WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.300
How does Catan Lens choose?

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.850
It scores every legal corner with a
handful of rules that strong players agree

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.280
on, and production comes first.

00:00:12.098 --> 00:00:14.188
Every number token carries dots.

00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:19.108
A six or an eight has five; a
two or a twelve has just one.

00:00:19.398 --> 00:00:22.238
The dots count the ways two
dice can roll that number,

00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:23.508
out of thirty-six.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:29.024
A corner collects from up to three hexes,
so its production is the sum of their

00:00:29.044 --> 00:00:29.844
dots.

00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:34.344
Wheat and ore count a little extra,
because they build cities and development

00:00:34.364 --> 00:00:35.174
cards.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.150
Resources that are rare on
this board are worth more.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.110
Smaller bonuses reward wood
with brick, wheat with ore,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.130
a harbour you can actually
feed, and room to grow.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.050
Repeating a number costs a little.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:51.698
Every rule traces back
to a published source:

00:00:51.988 --> 00:00:57.088
expert guides, champion interviews, and a
statistical study of four hundred online

00:00:57.108 --> 00:00:57.908
games.

00:00:58.588 --> 00:01:00.398
Placement is a snake draft.

00:01:00.688 --> 00:01:03.358
Projected placements plays
it out for every seat,

00:01:03.588 --> 00:01:07.798
so you can see what is likely to be
gone before your turn comes back.

00:01:08.008 --> 00:01:12.048
The suggested road steers away from
corners other players will probably take

00:01:12.068 --> 00:01:12.868
first.

00:01:13.427 --> 00:01:16.057
Drill mode turns all
of this into practice.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:21.397
First, set the table: how many players,
and whether you play Cities and Knights.

00:01:21.827 --> 00:01:26.957
Then climb sixteen levels, easy to hard,
with hints hidden until you commit.

00:01:27.636 --> 00:01:30.866
Miss, and you see your rank
and what the level needed,

00:01:31.136 --> 00:01:33.306
then get a fresh board at the same level.

00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:36.924
Find the best corner, and
the level is cleared.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:40.924
Later levels demand the exact
best corner on near-ties,

00:01:41.154 --> 00:01:44.024
from any seat, and for your
second settlement too.

00:01:44.842 --> 00:01:46.432
Playing at a real table?

00:01:46.922 --> 00:01:48.432
Copy your board in a minute.

00:01:48.982 --> 00:01:51.892
Pick a resource and tap
hexes to paint them,

00:01:52.322 --> 00:01:56.532
choose Numbers to set the tokens,
and tap the coast to place harbours.

00:02:01.545 --> 00:02:05.945
Every ranking now applies to your board,
and Copy link saves the whole thing,

00:02:05.965 --> 00:02:08.035
so you can share it with your table.

00:02:08.863 --> 00:02:10.793
But does the advice actually win?

00:02:11.123 --> 00:02:14.753
In forty thousand simulated
games between strong bots,

00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:20.273
openings chosen by Catan Lens won about as
often as the bots' own searched openings,

00:02:20.603 --> 00:02:24.173
and far more often than simply
grabbing the most dots.

00:02:25.226 --> 00:02:27.376
Catan Lens is free and open source.

00:02:27.726 --> 00:02:30.716
Try it in your browser,
or build on it on GitHub.
